From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Go7 port <go7-port@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] audio: primary: don't skip input transfers after a late
 one

When a transfer returns later than its wall-clock schedule,
StreamPrimary turns the next one into a buffer of zeros without
touching the stream. For output that drops data to catch up. For input
it inserts silence while the captured frames stay in the pipe, so each
late read adds a gap and a buffer of backlog that is never read back.

Skip only output transfers. An input stream catches up by reading what
has already been captured.
---
 audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp
index ac0d302..f91ea77 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ StreamPrimary::StreamPrimary(StreamContext* context, const Metadata& metadata)
             const long sleepTimeUs = std::min(totalOffsetUs, bufferDurationUs);
             LOG(VERBOSE) << __func__ << ": sleeping for " << sleepTimeUs << " us";
             usleep(sleepTimeUs);
-        } else {
+        } else if (!mIsInput) {
             mSkipNextTransfer = true;
         }
     } else {
